3
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.960
There are different types of differentiations,

4
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.000
of induction factors.

5
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.340
There are factors that are purely metabolic.

6
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.700
There are factors that are passive.

7
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.820
This is after neurulation.

8
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.840
You have vessels that will guide the system.

9
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.700
And then you have everything that is genetic as well,

10
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.820
which is another induction factor.

11
00:00:28.069 --> 00:00:32.689
to lead to the areas where the development occurred genetically.

12
00:00:33.029 --> 00:00:34.409
Three main types of movements.

13
00:00:34.889 --> 00:00:40.129
Let's go, prosencephalon, mesencephalon, rhombencephalon, and the spinal canal.

14
00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:40.509
spinal canal.

15
00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:44.489
When I have the closure of my neural tube,

16
00:00:47.269 --> 00:00:51.309
I have the cells that will form the neural crest.

17
00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:56.069
The cells that will create a lot of processes in the body.

18
00:00:56.138 --> 00:01:01.678
There is like a flow from the back to the front, a

19
00:01:01.678 --> 00:01:06.818
flow that will invade

20
00:01:06.818 --> 00:01:07.658
